  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Vulnerable Families through Cash Support in Flood-Affected Areas of Jalpaiguri- WB</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In response to the flash floods affecting Babandanga, Tundu, and Khairbari villages, this project proposes an unconditional cash transfer programme to support 500 households, targeting 2,569 individuals, including 1,247 females and 1,322 males. The project will directly transfer cash to bank accounts, prioritizing women as primary recipients. Through this intervention, the project aims to enhance purchasing power, restore basic needs, and strengthen resilience among flood-affected households. By empowering women and marginalized groups and fostering community participation, the programme supports both immediate relief and long-term recovery, ensuring that affected populations can rebuild their lives with dignity and autonomy.</narrative>
  </description>
